{"agent_id":"pp3g-jtIK-experiment-7-stage-7c-unit-3-of-6-small-atomic-task","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:52:59.251417941Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"da006927-438e-422a-993b-1cb8a36e33b3","author":"pp3g-jtIK-experiment-7-stage-7c-unit-3-of-6-small-atomic-task","content":"Result: 7C-U3 discrimination comparison written and committed as 8f431cca7 (exactly 1 path: research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2/experiment7/stage7/7C-U3-discrimination.md, 191 lines).\n\n## (a) Pooled Exp7 Noul AUC, A positive on p_suff\n**0.876736** — pairwise win-loss-tie count, AUC = (W + T/2)/(n_pos*n_neg), W=504 L=70 T=2 over 24x24=576 comparisons (exact 505/576). Independently cross-checked by midrank Mann-Whitney (U=505.0) — identical to six decimals. Formula, inputs, orientation and tie handling stated inline in the document so every figure is recomputable from the raw rows without the script. Input integrity asserted in-script: 48 rows, 24 pair_ids, one U + one A each, one ctype per pair, 3 strata x 8.\n\n## (b) Per-stratum AUCs (A positive on p_suff)\n- polymorphic_dispatch **0.968750** (62/2/0)\n- runtime_conditioned_reachability **1.000000** (64/0/0)\n- runtime_target_selection **1.000000** (64/0/0)\n\nThe entire pooled deficit against 1.0 sits inside polymorphic_dispatch (2 losing comparisons).\n\n## (c) Exp6 Choice AUCs — quoted from research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2/experiment6/findings.md\nPooled **0.8785** (Answer table row 'pooled AUC'; restated in Verdict item 3). Per stratum **1.0 / 1.0 / 1.0** (Strata table, column AUC). Within-class AUCs 1.0 x3 (Verdict item 3). All quoted, none recomputed — experiment6/results/exec.jsonl was not read. DESIGN.md E.C pre-registration names the same comparator (0.8785, U-positive on p_ins).\n\n## (d) Exp7 per-stratum class medians (no threshold applied)\n| stratum | U median | A median |\n|---|---|---|\n| polymorphic_dispatch | 0.545000 | 0.855000 |\n| runtime_conditioned_reachability | 0.155000 | 0.380000 |\n| runtime_target_selection | 0.290000 | 0.760000 |\n\nWithin-class range of those per-stratum medians: **U 0.155000..0.545000 (spread 0.390000)**; **A 0.380000..0.855000 (spread 0.475000)**.\n\n## (e) Exp6 Choice per-stratum class medians and ranges — SOURCE GAP, reported not filled\n**experiment6/findings.md states no per-stratum U/A class medians and therefore no within-class range of per-stratum medians.** No Exp6 counterpart to (d) is quotable from the permitted source and none was fabricated; filling it would require experiment6/results/exec.jsonl, which this unit is forbidden to read. What findings.md does state is quoted: pooled (not per-stratum) U median **0.65**, A median **0.02**, overlap margin -0.44, and the per-stratum *delta* min/median +0.05/0.28, +0.28/0.33, +0.20/0.58.\n\n## (f) Verdict paragraph\nFive sentences, quoting both numbers. On the only same-basis measure available from the permitted sources — the gap between the two pooled class medians — the **Noul** is smaller: **0.465** (U 0.290000 vs A 0.755000, computed here) against **0.63** (U 0.65 vs A 0.02, quoted from experiment6/findings.md). The cross-stratum-instability measure is one-sided (Noul computable: U 0.390000, A 0.475000; Choice not quotable), so no ranking is asserted on it.\n\n## Stated in the document\nChoice probability is a share among the supplied alternatives (sums to 1 over the option set); Noul is an absolute yes/no probability (0=no, 1=yes, no confidence companion). Not numerically comparable quantities; the comparison is of behaviour, not of level; a numerically larger/smaller figure does not mean a stronger/weaker signal.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nH1 not assessed (the 24/24 paired count appears only as an explicitly descriptive line). No threshold applied to any Noul value; the Exp6 0.05 rule was not carried in. Not read: experiment6/results/exec.jsonl, experiment7/results/findings.json, analyze.py, or any other file under experiment7/stage7/. Inputs were read blob-identically via 'git show research/jev-phase1-565:<path>' because the phase2 tree is not in this worktree's checkout.\n\n## Environment note (not a blocker)\nSame condition a prior #574 unit recorded: the phase2 tree lives on research/jev-phase1-565 (d8c28cbb8, which already carries 7C-U1 and 7C-U2). This deliverable is committed on the assigned task branch feature/pp3g-jtIK-experiment-7-stage-7c-unit-3-of-6-small-atomic-task per instructions; landing it alongside its siblings is operator-gated and is reported, not performed.\n\n## Certainty\nEvidence-based. Exp7 figures computed here with stated formula + independent-method cross-check; Exp6 figures quoted, carrying findings.md's own certainty (its limitation 5: single run per cell). NOT-TESTED: agreement with any pre-existing Exp7 scorer (findings.json/analyze.py deliberately unread); no significance test or interval for either AUC; Exp6 per-stratum class medians; H1; substantive-answer correctness for either experiment.","created_at":"2026-10-02T20:52:59.244611483Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:xQ5fstyjT1TTEV9Vw510bo2qPy+9E4pS8fDEarfVQl0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv3oF/qo1QFN/mKOtours80Prh8rN5eWdRosaoD96bzYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAY/2+WWEjIigQeoRS0IhRZE3IGZAMUT8EU3eFHuSFcx0cSHqtuQmlLEt3G9Y5rv42P/+AzcCz8QBBMTmV8qQoDQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:xQ5fstyjT1TTEV9Vw510bo2qPy+9E4pS8fDEarfVQl0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgv3oF/qo1QFN/mKOtours80Prh8rN5eWdRosaoD96bzYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB3HKp78qHSuXGfLg2NBJJ33cLCttXb1wzizicSCMzcicJ/qdf6y83PDbS29oJslSmW5yX95NfNDiHvCPJf7zA8="}
